  "cut_reasons": {
    "Cut a Deal": "Gives each opponent 2 cards in a 4-player game \u2014 net card disadvantage in Commander",
    "Elven Farsight": "One-shot scry 2 draw 1 \u2014 too low value, replaced with recurring engine",
    "Scale the Heights": "Conditional on having a land in hand and only draws 1 \u2014 replaced with Elemental Bond",
    "Zimone's Experiment": "One-shot look at 4 effect \u2014 replaced with Guardian Project for recurring draw",
    "Dryad Greenseeker": "Slow tap-for-maybe-a-land \u2014 replaced with Garruk's Packleader for draw-on-ETB",
    "Manalith": "Weakest ramp piece at 3 mana for 1 mana \u2014 replaced with Forest to reach 38 lands; Raucous Audience fills explosive ramp role better",
    "Cliffhaven Sell-Sword": "2/1 for 2 mana is the weakest vanilla 2-drop with 8 others already in deck \u2014 replaced with 3-drop Orazca Frillback",
    "Thornhide Wolves": "3/4 for 5 mana fails the CMC 4-5 bar \u2014 replaced with Gigantosaurus 10/10",
    "Axebane Stag": "3/4 for 7 mana catastrophically fails the 6+ CMC bar \u2014 replaced with Whiptail Wurm 8/5",
    "Kindercatch": "6/6 for triple-G unreliable in 2-color, pales next to Quakestrider 12/8 \u2014 replaced with Enormous Baloth 7/7",
    "Quilled Slagwurm": "7/7 for triple-G worse than every other high-CMC vanilla option \u2014 replaced with Cowl Prowler 6/6",
    "Serra's Blessing": "Gives all creatures Vigilance \u2014 vanilla creatures gain an ability and lose Jasmine's evasion, directly breaks the strategy",
    "Oakenform": "Aura risks 2-for-1; counter sub-theme now handles buffing more reliably",
    "Desecration Plague": "Redundant enchantment removal \u2014 Naturalize already fills this role cheaper",
    "Besotted Knight // Betroth the Beast": "Has adventure ability \u2014 doesn't benefit from commander evasion, replaced with recurring draw",
    "Cheeky House-Mouse // Squeak By": "Has adventure ability \u2014 doesn't benefit from commander evasion, replaced with recurring draw",
    "Fang-Druid Summoner": "Has ETB ability \u2014 doesn't benefit from commander evasion, replaced with recurring draw",
    "Ajani's Response": "4WW for situational damage prevention \u2014 replaced with Gravity Well for permanent ongoing anti-flying protection",
    "Wildest Dreams": "Requires X+X+G and a stocked graveyard \u2014 too situational and mana-intensive, replaced with Runic Armasaur for passive recurring draw",
    "Three Visits": "One-shot Forest fetch \u2014 replaced with Selvala, Heart of the Wilds for recurring mana equal to greatest power creature",
    "Pillar Launch": "Combat trick +2/+2 reach untap \u2014 replaced with Oak Street Innkeeper for passive hexproof on all tapped creatures during opponents' turns",
    "Ballynock Trapper": "4 mana 2/2 tapper \u2014 fails CMC 4 bar, has abilities so no commander synergy, replaced with Rootborn Defenses for instant-speed board protection",
    "Path to Exile": "Exile lets opponent send commander to command zone and recast \u2014 replaced with Kenrith's Transformation which locks commander on battlefield permanently and draws a card",
    "Druid of the Cowl": "Basic 2/3 tap for G \u2014 replaced with Incubation Druid which taps for 3 mana with a counter, guaranteed by Good-Fortune Unicorn on ETB",
    "Guardian Project": "Replaced by Elemental Bond which covers the same draw role at a fraction of the price ($3.83 vs $17.29)",
    "Kalonian Tusker": "Worst rate 2-drop at GG for a 2/2 \u2014 replaced with Ruxa which provides anthem, damage-through-blockers, and recursion for vanilla creatures",
    "Scale Up": "Trample redundant \u2014 Jasmine blocks ability-creature blockers and Ruxa already pushes full damage through any blocker",
    "Garruk's Gorehorn": "7/3 at CMC 5 \u2014 terrible toughness, replaced by Terrian 9/7 at same CMC",
    "Primordial Wurm": "Near-duplicate of Vorstclaw (both 4GG ~7/6) \u2014 replaced by Tuinvale Treefolk which breaks redundancy and adds adventure counter synergy"
  },
